    "methods_description": "Recordings were obtained from eight epidural contacts placed alongside the dorsal cervical spinal cord in each patient, with the fourth contact (from caudal) as reference and a ground wire twisted around the wire for the sixth contact. In each trial, an auditory cue preceded electric median nerve stimulation at the left wrist, with the cue-to-stimulus interval either fixed (1100 ms) or randomly varied (100-2100 ms) across alternating blocks. Subjects silently counted rare trials containing two rapid-succession stimuli (80 ms ISI) and reported the count at block end.",
